#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
msgid ""
"Okay.  What about the steel grade?  Tempering will make your weapon much more"
" durable and a little sharper."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
msgid "No, high carbon steel is fine."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
msgid "[+50 merch, +2 days] Yes, tempered steel would be excellent."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
msgid ""
"Great, so I can make your "
"<item_name:<u_val:general_artisans_blacksmith_weapon>> for "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_weapon_cost> merch and in "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_weapon_wait> days.  Deal?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
msgid ""
"[<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_weapon_cost> merch] Deal.  See you in "
"<u_val:number_artisans_blacksmith_weapon_wait> days."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_cody_weaponsmith.json
msgid "It's all done!  Sorry for the long wait; hopefully it's worth it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"You hit the nail on the head.  You bring me cartridges of one type, and I "
"reload them into another.  Ammo has its own exchange rate, for example, you "
"can exchange a hundred rifle rounds for three hundred pistol rounds or vice "
"versa."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"Alright.  So, first you give me your rounds, I'll put them on your account, "
"and then I can reload them in another caliber of your choice.  What ammo do "
"you want to convert?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"\n"
"\n"
"[Your credit: $<u_val:number_artisans_gunsmith_credit>]"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/dialog_statue.json
msgid "That's all for now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Now I want you to convert these rounds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"[<color_light_green>+$30</color>, <color_light_red>-100 "
"<item_name:46mm></color>]"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Sorry, but you need to get me any other ammo first."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "Sure.  What do you want me to convert your ammo to?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"Alright, that's <item_name:<u_val:general_artisans_gunsmith_ammo>>.  I can "
"reload about 200 rounds in one day.  How many do you need?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"[-$<u_val:number_artisans_gunsmith_sum0>, 50 rounds, 6 hours] See you later."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"[-$<u_val:number_artisans_gunsmith_sum1>, 200 rounds, 1 day] See you later."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"[-$<u_val:number_artisans_gunsmith_sum3>, 600 rounds, 3 days] See you later."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid ""
"[-$<u_val:number_artisans_gunsmith_sum5>, 1000 rounds, 5 days] See you later."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "I changed my mind, let's look at the list again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_convert.json
msgid "The conversion is complete, here is your ammunition."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I'd like to convert some rounds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "How's the 'printing' thing going?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Next series of currency gotta be ready in around <interval>, fresh off the "
"print!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid "I'll make sure to take a look.  <end_talking_bye>"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_jay_dialogue.json
msgid ""
"Where did you… I- I don't know what to say.\"  Jay takes the rifle reverently.  \"What did they do to this thing?  The receiver's all chopped up!\"  He turns it over so carefully that you could mistake him for holding a child instead of a gun.  \"This thing was beautiful.  Modern rails, ergonomic furniture, recoil balancing system… At least it's all still here.  I know Cody thinks that she did something wrong, but all I remember is being so angry… just blindingly furious.  Then I was running.  When I woke up, everything was fine.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Thank you for letting me see this, and for getting Cody and I talking.  If you could help me out with something for Cody, I'll make this rifle right, and hook you up with a casket mag and a box of the good ammo for it.  Stuff from my reserves."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find the debug software"
#: data/json/npcs/isolated_road/isolated_road_missions.json
msgid "Thanks bud, I'll take it from here.  Take care of that rifle, now."
msgstr ""

